# Line endings, settled here rather than per machine.
#
# Without this file, how a checkout looks depends on each developer's
# `core.autocrlf` setting. This machine has it on, so the repository already
# holds LF and only the working copy is CRLF — but a contributor or a CI runner
# with a different setting would start committing CRLF, and the diff would show
# every line of a file as changed when nothing had.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text; `eol=lf` fixes what text looks like
# in the repository. Windows editors handle LF fine, and Phase 6's CI runs on
# Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. Never normalised, never diffed as text — the convergence plots in
# reports/ are the immediate case.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# Resolver output, not hand-written. Marking it generated collapses it by
# default in GitHub diffs and keeps it out of the language statistics, so a
# 1,274-line lockfile does not drown a review.
uv.lock linguist-generated=true

# Documentation is the substance of this project, not an afterthought — count
# it in the language statistics rather than hiding it.
docs/**/*.md linguist-documentation=false
